#################### Step 10: Second Switch #################### 

The second Switch receives the frame.

It checks only:

Destination MAC

Finds PC2 in its MAC Table.

Forwards the frame only to PC2.

#################### Step 11: PC2 Receives the SYN #################### 

PC2 receives the frame.

It removes the Ethernet Header.

IP checks:

Destination IP

192.168.2.20

↓

This is my IP.

The packet is passed to TCP.

TCP checks:

Destination Port

22

The operating system has an SSH server listening on TCP Port 22.

TCP creates a new connection entry.

TCP State becomes:

SYN-RECEIVED
#################### Step 12: TCP Three-Way Handshake #################### 

PC2 sends:

SYN + ACK

The packet travels:

PC2

↓

Switch

↓

Router

↓

Switch

↓

PC1

At every router:

Ethernet Header is removed.
TTL is decremented.
IP checksum is recalculated.
A new Ethernet Header is created.

PC1 receives the SYN-ACK.

PC1 sends:

ACK

Again it travels through:

PC1

↓

Switch

↓

Router

↓

Switch

↓

PC2

Now both systems enter the TCP state:

ESTABLISHED

The TCP connection is now ready.

#################### Step 13: SSH Starts

Only after TCP is established does SSH begin.

SSH performs:

Version Exchange
Algorithm Negotiation
Key Exchange
Server Authentication
User Authentication
Session Key Generation

Now both systems have an encrypted channel.

#################### Step 14: SCP Transfers the File

SCP now sends:

File Name
File Size
File Permissions
File Data

SSH encrypts all the data.

TCP splits the encrypted data into multiple segments.

Each segment follows the same path:

PC1
↓

Switch
↓

Router
↓

Switch
↓

PC2

PC2:

TCP reassembles all segments.
SSH decrypts the data.
SCP reconstructs the original file.
The operating system writes the file to the destination path.
Interview Summary

✅ Switch forwards using MAC addresses.

✅ Router forwards using IP addresses.

✅ ARP resolves an IP address to a MAC address on the local network.

✅ TCP establishes a reliable connection using the three-way handshake.

✅ SSH provides encryption and authentication.

✅ SCP uses the secure SSH channel to transfer the file.

✅ IP addresses remain the same end-to-end, while MAC addresses change at every routed hop. This is the exact flow you can explain confidently in networking interviews.









