Interview Summary
Ping uses ICMP, not TCP or UDP.
There is no TCP three-way handshake.
The IP layer decides whether the destination is on the same subnet or a different subnet.
ARP resolves the next-hop MAC address.
Switches forward based on MAC addresses.
Routers forward based on IP addresses, decrement TTL, and create a new Ethernet frame for each hop.
IP addresses remain unchanged end-to-end, while MAC addresses change at every routed hop.